From: Stained Glass OS contributors
Subject: shell32: a drive's menu -- Open first, Eject for discs and removable drives

A drive item had no file type, so its menu's first, default item came from
whatever the buffer held ("shell"); it offered Cut and Delete and no Eject, so
a disc could not be ejected from File Explorer -- a mounted disc keeps the
drive's tray locked. Drives open as folders; Cut and Delete go; Eject, for a
CD/DVD or removable drive, runs sg-session's sg-eject (unmount, then eject,
through UDisks2, reporting its exit status) and otherwise sends
IOCTL_STORAGE_EJECT_MEDIA.

